 "   \"read\": \"src/broadcastread.js readBroadcast(env, reader, q), q = {eval?} (a URLSearchParams or the MCP arguments); equippedHere(env, reader, project?) is its equipped-here region alone, the SAME function GET /map/mcp's workspace-shelf reads\",",
 "   \"verbs\": \"sprint 3, D2 (B7): src/broadcast.js publishAnswer(env, person, {id, confirm?, eval?}, {press?}) and equipAnswer(env, person, {slug, v, project?, confirm?, eval?}, {press?}) are the ONE function of each verb, called by the MCP tools publish and equip (src/mcp.js) and their REST twins POST /broadcast/publish and POST /broadcast/equip; each checks who may call it (mayPublish / mayEquip: the role CLASS, a Partner refused), then without confirm answers the preview (planPublish / planEquip: every check, nothing written) and with confirm (or a signed-in browser's own press) files through publishItem / equipItem, each ONE filing through core.js fileTransmission's internal argument (the only writer of kind publish and kind equip)\",",
 "   \"live\": \"src/broadcastlive.js readLive(env, reader, q), q = {eval?, since?}: ONE statement, src/hotsql.js BROADCAST_LIVE_SQL (the page and GET /broadcast/live) or BROADCAST_POLL_SQL (?since=, the poll); liveKit() the drawing the server and the client share; renderLive the region\",",
 "   \"starter\": \"src/starter.js: PRESETS (src/presetdata.js, GENERATED), starterShelf(heres, ctx) the starter-shelf cards, presetRef/presetSource/starterDoc the names the equip door writes; src/broadcastread.js modelOf reads the project's preset equips off BROADCAST_SQL's rows (no new statement)\"",
 "  },",
 "  \"kinds\": {",
 "   \"item\": \"the draft, filed by a person's own Claude with file: lane leader, kind item, what (its name), why (one line), touches exactly one of skill | agent | workflow, gapRefs [\\\"item/<slug>\\\"] (slug [a-z0-9-]{2,40}), proof its source (an http(s) link or /artifact/<id>). Graded before the lane gates: complete routes auto, else incomplete with missing (the reply's example carries the call)\",",
 "   \"publish\": \"RESERVED: ONE row per press, lane leader, parent the item, the item's project, gapRefs [\\\"item/<slug>\\\"]; version n of a slug = its n-th publish; a slug belongs to its first publisher; routes auto\",",
 "   \"equip\": \"RESERVED: ONE row per press, lane leader, parent the publish row (= the version), project the equipping project, gapRefs [\\\"item/<slug>\\\"]; append-only, so update-version files a NEW row and the old one stands; 'equipped here' = the newest equip row of a slug in the project; routes auto Sprint 2: a STARTER item's equip has NO parent (the item is the engine's, not a filing): gapRefs [\\\"preset/<slug>\\\"], touches its kind, proof \\\"preset:<slug>@v<version>\\\" (the version it copied); 'equipped here' = the newest such row of the slug in the project\",",
 "   \"reserved\": \"kind publish and kind equip as a contribution item of preview and file: refused reserved_kind, nothing filed\"",
 "  },",
 "  \"call\": \"transmission.js FILING_ITEM_CALL: preview {items: [{contribution: {lane: \\\"leader\\\", kind: \\\"item\\\", what, why, touches: [\\\"skill\\\" | \\\"agent\\\" | \\\"workflow\\\"], gapRefs: [\\\"item/<slug>\\\"], proof: \\\"<http(s) link | /artifact/:id>\\\"}}]}, then file_contribution; then publish {id} (the preview), publish {id, confirm: true}\",",
 "  \"query\": \"?eval=1 (the suites' rows); the tool takes eval as an argument\",",
 "  \"shape\": \"{ project:{key, name}, org, stamp:{counts:{published, equippedHere, updates, starter}}, filter:{kinds:[{kind, count}] (skill, agent, workflow)}, regions:{shelf:[{slug, kind, v, what, why, source|null, publisher:{id, name}, publishedAt, equippedIn, here:{v|null, state:'none'|'current'|'update', by, at}, can:{equip, update, reason}, warning, href}], 'equipped-here':[{slug, kind, v, latest, state, by, at, href:'/contribution/<equip id>', source:'org'|'starter', title?, doc?:'starter/<slug>.md'}], 'org-wall-note':{org, text}, 'starter-shelf':[{slug, kind, title, purpose, calls:[tool], v, source:'starter', href:'/broadcast/starter/<slug>', equipSlug:'preset:<slug>', here:{v|null, state:'none'|'current'|'update', by, at, doc, href}, can:{equip, update, reason}}]}, mine:[{id, slug, kind, what, published:v|null, publishable, reason}], call, empty:{shelf?, 'equipped-here'?, mine?}, more?, eval?, live?:'unreachable' }\",",
 "  \"scope\": \"the shelf is org-wide (this worker's D1 alone: nothing crosses the org wall); equippedIn counts only the projects the reader holds a seat on (the owner: every active project) and an equip row in any other project is never read; mine is the reader's own drafts; the project is GET /goals' own (goalsread.js contextOf); suite rows out unless ?eval=1\",",
 "  \"shelf\": \"one card per published slug, newest publish first; v, what, why, kind and source are the newest publish's item (source only when it is an http(s) link or an /artifact/ id, verbatim: a renderer escapes it); publisher the slug's first publisher; here the newest equip of the slug in this project, pinned to its version: none, current (v = the newest) or update (a newer version waits); can.equip exactly when the reader is seated here and the state is none, can.update exactly when seated and the state is update, else a reason; warning is D8's fixed line 'Adds <publisher>'s <kind> to <project>. Everyone seated here gets it.'\",",
 "  \"reads\": \"ONE D1 statement beyond the memoized auth, src/hotsql.js BROADCAST_SQL (kinds item, publish and equip on idx_transmission_kind_eval, newest 2001, equips only in the reader's visible projects, plus the reader's active seats as UNION rows); GET /map/mcp runs the same one statement. The org's name is its row (src/tenant.js, once a minute per isolate). No migration. Sprint 2: the starter shelf reads nothing more (the bytes ride the bundle; the project's preset equips are rows of the same statement); the page adds the live picture's ONE statement (GET /broadcast/live's), so the HTML face runs two and the JSON face one\",",
 "  \"empty\": {",
