 "   \"equipped-here\": \"This project has equipped nothing.\",",
 "   \"mine\": \"You have no draft to publish. Your own Claude files one with the call below. (the call is the answer's call)\"",
 "  },",
 "  \"verbs\": {",
 "   \"auth\": \"sprint 3, D2 (B7; MCP.md §5 supersedes Q60CCC574): the MCP tools publish and equip, and their REST twins (auth bearer, below the gate: a key or a session; a read-only credential 403 read_only_credential, a cross-origin session 403 cross_origin_session_write, a ?k= key or no credential 401). Who: publish anyone whose role CLASS is not Partner, on their own draft, seated somewhere (the admin needs no seat); equip anyone whose role class is not Partner into a project they are seated on (the admin: any active project); a Partner (role partner, or a typed outside label) is 403 partner_refused before anything is read. Preview first: without confirm: true the answer is the preview {preview:true, verb, line, shows, reaches, text, next} and nothing is written; a signed-in browser's press on the Broadcast page is its own confirm\",",
 "   \"publish\": \"publish {id, confirm?, publishOnConfirm?} · POST /broadcast/publish {id, confirm?}: anyone seated in the org but a Partner, only on their own draft. 422 id_required · 404 unknown_item · 403 not_yours · 403 not_seated · 403 partner_refused · 422 incomplete_item · 409 already_published · 409 slug_taken\",",
 "   \"equip\": \"equip {slug, v, project?, confirm?, equipOnConfirm?} · POST /broadcast/equip {slug, v, project?, confirm?}: serves equip and update-version; anyone seated on the target project (the owner on any active one); project defaults to the request's own. 403 not_seated · 404 unknown_item · 404 unknown_version · 409 already_current · 422 project_required. Sprint 2: a Partner is 403 partner_refused. {slug: 'preset:<slug>', v, project?} equips a STARTER item at the engine's version (any other v: 404 unknown_version with latest; an unknown slug 404 unknown_item): it writes the project's COPY first, the item's body as the doc starter/<slug>.md through the knowledge write door (its k_docs row and ONE ledger row, kind knowledge; refused as that door refuses: project_forbidden, invalid_ops), then ONE equip filing (parent none, gapRefs [\\\"preset/<slug>\\\"], proof preset:<slug>@v<n>); 409 already_current when the project's newest equip of it is that version; a later edit of the copy is the project's own (preview then save_knowledge kind doc on that path), and Update re-copies it\",",
 "   \"reply\": \"JSON: publish {id, slug, v, item}, equip {id, slug, v, project, from}; a form is sent (303) to /broadcast?published=<id> or /broadcast?equipped=<id>; a starter equip also {doc:'starter/<slug>.md', knowledge:<the copy's ledger id>} and its form is sent to /broadcast?equipped=<id>&doc=<path>\"",
 "  },",
 "  \"unreachable\": \"a failed ledger statement answers 200 with live:'unreachable', empty regions and null counts; a D1 quota error propagates\",",
 "  \"auth\": \"GET /broadcast is in GATED_SURFACE: a caller with no credential is sent to /login (302), never answered the shelf. In UI-B11a a browser gets the JSON\",",
 "  \"resources\": [",
 "   \"brain://broadcast\"",
 "  ],",
 "  \"starter\": \"the twelve items built into the engine, in shelf order, the same for every org (no D1 read: the bytes ride the bundle); here is the project's NEWEST preset equip of the slug (none, current = the engine's version, update = an older one); can.equip exactly when the reader is seated here (the owner: any active project), not a Partner, and the state is none; can.update the same when the state is update; a Partner's reason is 'A Partner works on the projects they are seated on; equipping is a member's press.'\",",
 "  \"live\": {",
 "   \"door\": \"GET /broadcast/live (JSON); the Broadcast page draws the same read (data-region live-picture) in its first paint, never the JSON of GET /broadcast\",",
 "   \"read\": \"ONE statement on idx_transmission_project: the project's LANDED filings (route auto, or decided approve) of the last 7 days, newest 200, kinds counter, critique, rank, restore, item, publish and equip out (a press or a dispute, never work toward a goal), sharingu's own namespace out, suite rows out unless ?eval=1; each with its person (people by key, avatar after migrate-044) and its goal's title (k_goals by key)\",",
 "   \"shape\": \"{project:{key}|null, days:7, since:<ISO cutoff | ?since>, at:<the newest created_at seen, else since>, limit, more, people:[{id, name, initials, tone, n}] (the most first), goals:[{ref|null, title, known, n}] (the goals in the tree, the most fed first, then refs not in the tree, then the unaligned row: ref null, title 'Unaligned'), dots:[{id, by, goal, at, kind, what}] (oldest first), poll?:true, eval?:true, live?:'unreachable'}\",",
 "   \"poll\": \"?since=<ISO time>: the same rows from then on (>=, the client drops ids it holds), oldest first, at most 50, poll:true; the page polls on focus and every 30 s while visible, never on load, and flies what is new\",",
 "   \"page\": \"people left (avatar, name, count; past nine, one folded row), the goals they named right (title, count, the newest contributions as dots under it; the unaligned row quiet and last), one curve per person and goal (its width by count), every dot a link to /contribution/<id>; replayed on open under html.u-motion (each dot travels its curve, staggered by filing time, under a second, the goal pinging as dots land), hover or focus on a person or a goal dims the rest; reduced motion: no travel; the same picture as a list (data in a details, a phone's whole surface, the curves hidden)\"",
 "  }",
