 "   \"brain://map/{plane}\",",
 "   \"brain://map/node/{ref}\",",
 "   \"brain://goal/{ref}\",",
 "   \"brain://doc/{path}\",",
 "   \"brain://brief/{ref}\"",
 "  ],",
 "  \"resourceRefusal\": \"resources/read answers JSON-RPC error -32003 with the message 'project_forbidden: <note>'; resources/list and resources/templates/list descriptions say 'Add ?project=<key>' (additive)\",",
 "  \"twinRefusal\": \"a GET twin naming a project the caller may not read answers 403 JSON { error:'project_forbidden', project, seats, note, example? }\",",
 "  \"restWrite\": \"U-MCP-tail-c N2 (QE6B9CEBA): POST /grade (submit_grade's REST twin) scopes by its JSON body `project` through the SAME helper as the tool (src/mcp.js projectCallScope): a named project the caller may not read answers 403 JSON { error:'project_forbidden', project, seats, note, example? } and nothing is filed or counted; a readable named project grades on its re-scoped env; no `project` keeps the seam's scope. GET /updates calls the updates tool itself (src/mcp.js callTool), so its scope IS the tool's.\",",
 "  \"input\": \"U-MCP-tail-b D3 (QE6B9CEBA, Q952CAE10): src/core.js projectArg(v) is the ONE parse of a `project` argument at every door (resolveProject, doorProject, ask, POST /broadcast/equip, the wrap-up, the answer entries, round): undefined, null and \\\"\\\" are none; a string is trimmed and lower-cased; any other shape (object, array, number, boolean) is refused project_forbidden (not-allowed; nothing read or filed; `seats` listed; note \\\"`project` is one project key, a string\\\") — never coerced, never a 500\",",
 "  \"liveStamp\": \"U-MCP-tail-b D4: the session stamp defaults a read (resolveProject), fills an unnamed write (doorProject) and is the activeProject of whoami and updates ONLY while live (src/core.js liveStampOf: one of the caller's seats, or for the owner an ACTIVE project); an owner's stamp on an archived project is none — whoami, initialize and start-here bytes are unchanged for every live stamp\",",
 "  \"answerProject\": \"U-MCP-tail-b D5: one project per answer call (respond, round; REST and MCP): the entries' `project` and the call's top-level `project` name one project (or none), else project_forbidden with nothing filed; a named project goes through resolveProject and the qid is validated against THAT project's pack, the one the answer is stamped into\",",
 "  \"packProject\": \"U-MCP-tail-b D6 (healed: the adversarial review's finding 2): the project of read, changes and submit_grade's check_results row is the request's scope (the request's scope, src/project.js: the scope, or a single-project org's one project, else null — the org level); nothing a client sends besides `project` names the project, so no claim moves a grade or a read. With no project (a caller seated nowhere in a multi-project org) submit_grade is refused project_required and nothing is filed (check_results.project is a project key); a grade whose filing stamp differs from the project it reads is refused project_required naming it (example), so the grade row and its filing always agree\",",
 "  \"readProject\": \"U-MCP-tail-b D7: the brief of your own items (briefCountFor: every page's badge; updates' `yours` and GET /updates, in doors already) and GET /missing's ledger half read the request's scope (src/project.js projectOf / projectScopeOf, the rule home.js and the pack door read by), never the raw session stamp: a scope filters `project = ?`; an org with ONE active project filters `project = ?` on it (the project every door's default reads, so a tool equals its twin); a multi-project org's null scope (seated nowhere, not the owner) filters `project IS NULL`, never org-wide; an org with no active project row has no filter (byte-identical)\",",
 "  \"multiProject\": \"U-MCP-tail-b heal (the adversarial review's finding 1): ONE rule decides \\\"multi-project\\\" for the workspace seam (whether a request is scoped) and for projectScopeOf (a null scope's filter) and a seatless write's stamp (doorProject): src/core.js orgProjectsOnce — the D1 ACTIVE projects, through one memo (a minute per isolate, keyed by the D1 binding, pinned per request; /control's project writes drop it), so the seam and the reads never disagree\",",
 "  \"outOfScope\": \"eagle_* (org-wide); save_file's screen canon (stampProjectLoose); the stamp-narrowed views that read the sync session stamp by name (build, read_file, /audit, the / picker's presence test)\",",
 "  \"switcherChip\": \"U-TOPBAR: the top bar's project chip names the project the page read (the seam's resolveProject scope: named ?project=, the live stamp, or a member's single-seat/first-readable default); the owner's unnamed default is the org rollup and reads 'All projects'; ?project= never writes the stamp; Map · Arch hands the shell its arch plane's org-worker `projects` (U-MCP-tail-c N0), so its chip reads what every other page reads\",",
 "  \"refusal\": \"project_forbidden\"",
