 " },",
 " \"refusalClasses\": {",
 "  \"_doc\": \"Q939178BC: the refusal vocabulary collapses to this small, closed set. tools/make-door-contract.py computes each door's own `refusals` (which of these it can return) mechanically from its auth/owner/write fields, and refuses any declared error `class` outside this set — a caller handles three shapes, never fifty-eight.\",",
 "  \"not-authenticated\": {",
 "   \"meaning\": \"No valid credential reached this door — no session cookie, and no valid Authorization: Bearer token resolved to a person (a key in the address signs no one in).\",",
 "   \"nextAction\": \"Authenticate — sign in, send a valid bearer token, or a valid reader key — then retry the exact same call.\"",
 "  },",
 "  \"not-allowed\": {",
 "   \"meaning\": \"The caller authenticated fine, but its role, scope, or ownership may not do this specific thing (an owner-only door, a read-only OAuth grant on a write tool, a credential that doesn't own the resource).\",",
 "   \"nextAction\": \"Do not retry unchanged — this is a role/scope/ownership gate, not a transient failure. Use a credential that holds the right role or scope, or ask its holder.\"",
 "  },",
 "  \"not-found\": {",
 "   \"meaning\": \"The door authenticated the caller fine, but the id/ref/key asked for does not exist, or isn't visible to this caller.\",",
 "   \"nextAction\": \"Check the id/ref for a typo or staleness; do not retry the exact same call unchanged.\"",
 "  }",
 " },",
 " \"signIn\": {",
 "  \"_doc\": \"THE sign-in rule (D1b, 2026-10-02): ONE rule answers a caller no credential resolved for, on every door, decided in ONE place (src/util.js isBrowserNavigation and signInOr401). Before it, 25 gated pages sent a script with no key to the sign-in page (302) while their checks expected 401.\",",
 "  \"browserNavigation\": \"Sec-Fetch-Dest document, or Sec-Fetch-Mode navigate, or (from a client that sends neither) an Accept whose FIRST type is text/html — AND no Authorization header\",",
 "  \"navigation\": \"302 to /login?next=<the path and query asked for, never ?k=> (a form POST: next is the page the form lives on)\",",
 "  \"otherwise\": \"401 JSON {error, hint} — a request that asks for JSON, carries a bearer header (a bad key is a key: 401, never a page), or is a script or a fetch\",",
 "  \"idDoors\": \"a door that takes an id answers who is asking BEFORE it looks the id up: signed out, a real id and a made-up one get the same answer; signed in, an id the caller may not read answers not_found exactly as a missing one\",",
 "  \"mcp\": \"POST /mcp is a JSON-RPC door: no credential is a JSON-RPC error, never a page\"",
 " },",
 " \"orgArgument\": {",
 "  \"_doc\": \"sprint 7, 7.5a (docs/plan/PLATFORM.md §2 items 8 and 9: one /mcp; the OAuth grant carries the person and the org; whoami lists the orgs and a call switches between them). STATELESS: nothing is stored on a grant; each call names its org.\",",
 "  \"argument\": \"orgSlug: an optional string on EVERY tool (src/index.js ORG_ARG), and ?orgSlug= in a brain:// resource's uri — an org's path name as whoami's orgs lists it; left out, the credential's current org\",",
 "  \"grants\": \"an OAuth sign-in proved by the ACCOUNT's passphrase makes an ACCOUNT grant (props {personId, accountId, org, scope, cred}: the chosen seat, the account, that seat's org as the grant's current org, the account passphrase's stamp); one proved by a seat's OWN secret makes a SEAT grant (props {personId, scope, cred}: that seat alone — the shape of every grant made before 7.5a, so a client connected before it acts as its seat, unchanged). src/oauthgrants.js\",",
 "  \"reach\": \"an ACCOUNT grant acts, per call, as the account's own ACTIVE seat in the org named, with that seat's role (never more than the account's seats); a SEAT grant, a bearer key, a session or a read-only credential acts as its one seat: it may name only that seat's org\",",
 "  \"refusal\": \"org_unreachable — any other org (a seat's credential naming another org; an account grant naming an org it holds no active seat in, or one org per JSON-RPC batch): refused before anything is read or written, the same answer whether the org exists or not, listing only the orgs this credential reaches\",",
 "  \"ends\": \"an ACCOUNT grant ends when the account's passphrase changes (its stamp); a SEAT grant when that seat's key or passphrase changes (its stamp); a grant carrying NO stamp (made before G2) is refused outright, 401 invalid_token with the re-connect words (7.5b); either when the seat that keys it in the grant store is rotated, re-passworded or removed (src/oauthgrants.js revokeOAuthGrants)\",",
 "  \"whoami\": \"orgs: [{slug, name, role, current}] (an account grant: every org its account holds an active seat in; any other credential: its one org) and orgNote (how a call picks one)\",",
 "  \"doors\": [",
 "   \"whoami\"",
 "  ]",
 " },",
 " \"shapes\": {",
 "  \"_doc\": \"additive (sprint 3, B1; docs/plan/MCP.md §9 demand 2): the contribution shapes. ONE declaration, src/shapes.js SHAPES (a shape per lane of src/lanes.js), read by the filing doors, read, the contribution's page, the `formats` read and this contract (its fields, examples and places are GENERATED into `formats.shapes`). The fields new in B1 are each optional and checked at the door before anything is read or written: source, depends, open, next on every shape; audience, claim, channel, experiment on the gtm shape. src/transmission.js gateGrade never reads them: a missing one is never a refusal and the grade's reasons are unchanged.\",",
